          "language": "en",
          "language_probability": 0.99560546875,
          "text": "Good morning everyone and thank you for joining today. In this short demonstration we are going to translate a video from English into another language while keeping the speaker's own voice and matching the lip movements to the new audio. The pipeline first extracts the audio and transcribes it with a speech recognition model. Then it translates each sentence, synthesizes the translated speech using a clone voice. And finally regenerates the mouth region so that it lines up with the new words. Everything you see here is produced by open source models running on graphics cards in a single server. The output is watermarked so that it is always clear the video has been generated by software. Let us look at how long each stage takes and how the result holds up.",
